And while acting —
Let not others learn his secret; let him discover the enemy's vulnerabilities;
Let him conceal his own exposed [weaknesses] like a tortoise [withdrawing] its limbs.

Those born in <s>Kaliṅga</s> and <s>Aṅga</s> are the best; those from the east, <s>Cedi</s>, and <s>Karūṣa</s>,
and those from <s>Dāśārṇa</s> and the western regions are considered middling;
those from <s>Saurāṣṭra</s> and <s>Pañcanada</s> are regarded as inferior to them;
but the strength, speed, and spirit of all are enhanced by training.

A commodities building and granary — with pillars of baked brick, with four halls, a single entrance, multiple floors, with open space between pillars for escape routes, [commodities buildings] on both sides;
a raw materials building — long, with many halls, walls enclosed by concentric enclosures;
the same, combined with an underground chamber, serves as an armory;
and he should have a prison constructed — with a separate judicial section, a section for high officials, with separate quarters for women and men, with well-guarded enclosures at the exits.

