KAZ08.5.27cd/ such an ally is won over with difficulty, and even when won, quickly becomes disaffected.
KAZ08.5.28ab/ An ally who has exerted himself or is worthy of honor but, through delusion, is not honored;
KAZ08.5.28cd/ or one who is honored but not as befitting, or restrained beyond his capacity;

Or, if one perceives: 'Having seized the recoverable [territory], I shall drain away his treasury, army, stockpiles, and defense arrangements; I shall exhaust the valuable content of his mines, timber forests, elephant forests, embankments, and trade routes; I shall weaken his subjects, drive them away, or win them over through employment;
those [subjects], the enemy will antagonize through counter-measures; or I shall make him [the object of] trade to the opposing faction; or I shall deliver to him an ally who is blocked [from acting];
or, stationed there, I shall counteract the harassments of his territory or of my own or my ally's territory by thieves and enemies; or I shall cause a deficiency in his ally or his refuge;
the [ally], estranged from the enemy, will be won over by his own kinsman; or, having honored him, I shall give him the territory —
thus the ally, risen from the treaty, will be mine for a long time' — then one should seize even a recoverable gain.
